      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you're describing sounds like a profound sense of depersonalization and derealization, which is a very heavy burden to carry. When you feel empty, the focus shouldn't be on \"finding\" who you were, but on gently noticing what is present in this moment. Try focusing on small, immediate sensations—the feeling of your feet on the floor, the temperature of the air—to anchor yourself to the present reality, however distant it may feel.",
      "source": "target",
